// Stability criteria — dated, pre-registered (METHODOLOGY R6, engine.md).
//
// GENERATION 1, registered 2026-07-31, for a scenario that did not exist before
// today. `version: 1` is this FILE's generation; every threshold in it is the
// corpus's generation-4 value, copied verbatim from data/scenarios/lr_00 and
// data/scenarios/tracer_2r without one digit changed.
//
//   NOT ONE THRESHOLD HERE WAS CHOSEN WITH KNOWLEDGE OF WHAT THIS SCENARIO DOES.
//   The tape and this file were written before the engine had ever been pointed
//   at solv_1g_money. Every number was fixed earlier, against the synthetic
//   healthy/sick series in tests/test_09_detectors.rs, to score a corpus this
//   world is not part of. If this scenario fails one of these, the finding is
//   that it fails a bar the rest of the corpus is already held to.
//
// WHAT THIS FILE ASSERTS: stability only — the metrics stayed inside a band and
// their wobble did not grow. IT DOES NOT ASSERT CORRECTNESS. Every class here
// passes on a world whose prices are arbitrarily wrong as long as they are wrong
// quietly: a run that instantly settles on RealWage = 0.02 and holds it scores
// LevelRange 1.00, RollingCv 0.00 and ResidualDamping 0.00 — a clean sweep.
// Whether the prices went to the RIGHT PLACE is equilibrium.ron's question, read
// by tests/test_12_solvable.rs, and B8's in the run certificate.
//
// THE DIFFERENCE FROM solv_1g's OTHERWISE IDENTICAL FILE. In solv_1g the DEAD
// and DRIFTING thresholds on Velocity are scoring an UNPINNED direction: one
// wealth tier means the price level is a free ray, and Velocity is proportional
// to the level. HERE THAT CAVEAT DOES NOT APPLY. Two tiers switch on the pop's
// cash band, the level has a closed form, and equilibrium Velocity is
// 2/(2*b_cash + 1) = 0.142857 exactly. So on this tape — and, as far as this
// corpus goes, only on the three two-tier solv_* tapes — a Velocity verdict is
// a verdict about something that has a right answer. That is not a reason to
// move a threshold; it is the reason the pair (solv_1g, solv_1g_money) exists.
//
// Equilibrium readings against each bar, all comfortably inside, all computed
// from the tape rather than measured: Velocity 0.1429 vs the 0.003 DEAD floor;
// Employment 1.0 vs 0.05; every RollingCv 0.00 vs 0.12; every LevelRange 1.00
// vs 2.2; every ResidualDamping 0.00 vs 1.5; Concentration 0.536 vs 0.82;
// RealIncome 13.0 vs 0.8; BldUtil 0.8 vs 0.05. A scenario that fails one of
// these has moved, and how far it moved is the measurement.
//
// WHY THE WINDOW IS 150..1000: copied from lr_00 unchanged. The transient is
// arguably zero here — mode A starts AT the equilibrium — but shortening the
// window would be a scenario-specific choice made by someone who knew the
// answer, and would stop these numbers being comparable with the corpus's.
//
// WHERE THE FIRST-PRINCIPLES JUSTIFICATION RUNS OUT, said plainly: the liveness
// floors (0.003, 0.05, 0.12, 0.82, 0.8, 0.60) are ported from
// notebooks/07_stability_suite.py, where they were global Python constants
// applied to every scenario. NOTHING DERIVES THEM. They are inherited, not
// justified, and this file does not pretend otherwise. The two that ARE
// evidenced are 2.2 and 1.5, fixed from the separation between synthetic healthy
// and sick series in tests/test_09_detectors.rs: healthy levels reach at most
// 1.81 and sick start at 2.69; healthy oscillation reaches 1.04 and sick starts
// at 1.99.
//
// CHANGING A THRESHOLD AFTER SEEING RESULTS REQUIRES A NEW DATED GENERATION,
// never a silent edit.
(
    version: 1,
    date: "2026-07-31",
    transient: 150,
    analysis_end: 1000,
    staple_good: "grain",
    labour_good: "labour",
    nan_policy: FailClosed,
    classes: [
        (
            name: "DEAD",
            fatal: true,
            metrics: [Velocity],
            rule: FracBelow(thresh: 0.003, frac: 0.80),
            window: Analysis,
            short_circuit: true,
        ),
        (
            name: "DEAD_EMPLOYMENT",
            fatal: true,
            metrics: [Employment],
            rule: FracBelow(thresh: 0.05, frac: 0.80),
            window: Analysis,
        ),
        (
            name: "UNSTABLE",
            fatal: true,
            metrics: [Velocity, Employment, RealWage],
            rule: RollingCv(window: 10, max_cv: 0.12),
            window: Analysis,
        ),
        (
            name: "DRIFTING",
            fatal: true,
            metrics: [Velocity, RealWage],
            rule: LevelRange(max_ratio: 2.2),
            window: Analysis,
        ),
        (
            name: "SWINGING",
            fatal: true,
            metrics: [Velocity, RealWage],
            rule: ResidualDamping(max_ratio: 1.5),
            window: Halves,
        ),
        (
            name: "CURRENCY_DRAIN",
            fatal: true,
            metrics: [Concentration],
            rule: MeanAndSlope(mean_min: 0.82, slope_min: 0.0),
            window: Analysis,
        ),
        (
            name: "POP_DESTITUTION",
            fatal: true,
            metrics: [RealIncome],
            rule: FracBelow(thresh: 0.8, frac: 0.50),
            window: Analysis,
        ),
        (
            name: "DEAD_BUILDING",
            fatal: false,
            metrics: [BldUtil],
            rule: FracBelow(thresh: 0.05, frac: 0.60),
            window: PostTransient,
        ),
    ],
)
